00:10:06.231 --> 00:10:09.735
All right, boys,
show us what you've brought.

248
00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:14.531
This is our new Ether-nopian,
Starvin' Marvin.

249
00:10:14.656 --> 00:10:16.325
He can do really
cool stuff with his voice.

250
00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:18.160
Show 'em, Starvin' Marvin.

251
00:10:18.285 --> 00:10:21.538
No, Starvin' Marvin,
that's Kenny's creamed corn.

252
00:10:21.663 --> 00:10:24.041
No, Starvin' Marvin,
that's a bad Starvin' Marvin!

253
00:10:24.166 --> 00:10:25.751
Boys,
what the hell are you doing?

254
00:10:25.876 --> 00:10:27.336
This is horribly,
horribly wrong.

255
00:10:27.461 --> 00:10:28.920
How did you get this child?

256
00:10:29.046 --> 00:10:30.255
He was accidentally
delivered to us

257
00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:31.840
instead
of a sports watch.

258
00:10:31.965 --> 00:10:33.550
The sports watch
from the commercial?

259
00:10:33.675 --> 00:10:35.719
Yeah, that one.
- I want a Starvin' Marvin.

260
00:10:35.844 --> 00:10:38.639
Me too.
- Yes, I'll pay $50 for one.

261
00:10:40.557 --> 00:10:42.976
Boys, you're too
young to take care of a child.

262
00:10:43.101 --> 00:10:44.686
I'm afraid I'm going
to have to call

263
00:10:44.811 --> 00:10:46.271
the Red
Cross and have him returned.

264
00:10:46.396 --> 00:10:47.773
Ah,
I told you we shouldn't have

265
00:10:47.898 --> 00:10:49.232
brought him to school dude.

266
00:10:49.358 --> 00:10:51.068
Okay, thank you very much.

267
00:10:51.193 --> 00:10:53.236
Yes, you can pick
him up tonight. Bye now.

268
00:10:53.362 --> 00:10:54.821
Now, boys, I hope
you've learned your lesson.

269
00:10:54.946 --> 00:10:56.281
No.

270
00:10:56.406 --> 00:10:57.741
You can't
care for this child!

271
00:10:57.866 --> 00:10:58.950
But I thought we were
supposed

272
00:10:59.076 --> 00:11:00.410
to care
on Thanksgiving.

273
00:11:00.535 --> 00:11:01.870
Yes,
but you don't actually get

274
00:11:01.995 --> 00:11:03.413
involved with
the child's lives.

275
00:11:03.538 --> 00:11:05.040
You're supposed
to just send money,

276
00:11:05.165 --> 00:11:06.291
and once in a while
they write you a letter.

277
00:11:06.416 --> 00:11:07.793
You see, Marvin didn't grow up

278
00:11:07.918 --> 00:11:09.294
in a normal
place like South Park.

279
00:11:09.419 --> 00:11:11.004
So why can't
he live here now?

280
00:11:11.129 --> 00:11:13.131
Because he can't!
- Because why?

281
00:11:13.256 --> 00:11:15.050
Because eight year
olds can't be parents!

282
00:11:15.175 --> 00:11:16.760
Then you take care of him.

283
00:11:16.885 --> 00:11:20.555
I can't.
I--Umm, I'm very busy.

284
00:11:20.681 --> 00:11:22.891
I send my $5 a month, see?

285
00:11:23.016 --> 00:11:25.686
This sucks,
Starvin' Marvin is our friend.

286
00:11:25.811 --> 00:11:27.437
Oh well, back
to the poor country with you.

287
00:11:27.562 --> 00:11:29.064
You better watch
what you say, Cartman!

288
00:11:29.189 --> 00:11:30.774
You might be poor
and hungry some day.

289
00:11:30.899 --> 00:11:32.776
Yeah, right.

290
00:11:34.945 --> 00:11:36.363
I knew that you
were the only person

291
00:11:36.488 --> 00:11:37.948
who would
listen to me, Chef.

292
00:11:38.073 --> 00:11:39.825
Yeah, well,
let's get it over with.

293
00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:42.369
This place gives
me the Bubujeebies.

294
00:11:42.494 --> 00:11:45.330
Look here in my microscope.
Tell me what you see.

295
00:11:45.455 --> 00:11:49.501
Uhh, I see
an extreme close-up

296
00:11:49.626 --> 00:11:52.170
of Vanessa Redgrave's
private parts.

297
00:11:52.295 --> 00:11:53.839
Oh, whoops.

298
00:11:53.964 --> 00:11:56.425
Now tell me what you see.

299
00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:58.552
Well, I'm no biologist,

300
00:11:58.677 --> 00:12:00.679
but I'd say it
looks like turkey DNA.

301
00:12:00.804 --> 00:12:03.223
Precisely, but look
how rapidly it's dividing.

302
00:12:03.348 --> 00:12:05.183
What does it mean?

303
00:12:05.308 --> 00:12:08.270
Means the turkeys are
growing at an exponential rate.

304
00:12:08.395 --> 00:12:11.606
If we don't destroy them all,
they'll take over the town.

305
00:12:11.732 --> 00:12:15.485
Maybe the world.
- Oh, fudge!

306
00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:18.947
Uhh, let me see that
Vanessa Redgrave thing again.

307
00:12:19.072 --> 00:12:21.366
Sure.

308
00:12:24.703 --> 00:12:27.497
Hello there, little boy,
we're looking for a starving

309
00:12:27.622 --> 00:12:29.666
African child who was
accidentally sent here instead

310
00:12:29.791 --> 00:12:33.044
of a Teiko sports watch.

311
00:12:37.716 --> 00:12:39.593
Hey, hey,
what's going on?

312
00:12:39.718 --> 00:12:42.512
Hey, let go of me!
Hey!

313
00:12:42.637 --> 00:12:44.431
Hey! I'll kick you in the nuts.
Okay, man?

314
00:12:44.556 --> 00:12:46.892
Here's your sports watch,
son, sorry for the mix-up.

315
00:12:47.017 --> 00:12:48.727
Hey! Hey, seriously!

316
00:12:48.852 --> 00:12:50.645
Hey, you're pissing me off!

317
00:12:50.771 --> 00:12:52.898
Sweet.

318
00:12:57.444 --> 00:12:59.529
So how does this thing work?

319
00:12:59.654 --> 00:13:01.323
Well mayor,
it's based on the cash grab,

320
00:13:01.448 --> 00:13:02.783
but instead of money,
the cans of food

321
00:13:02.908 --> 00:13:04.826
are blown around
inside the capsule.

322
00:13:04.951 --> 00:13:07.746
The pov inside catches as many
as he can to feed his family.

323
00:13:07.871 --> 00:13:10.624
Pov?
- Poverty stricken citizen.

324
00:13:10.749 --> 00:13:12.751
Oh-ho-ho, brilliant.

325
00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:20.342
What the hell is this?

326
00:13:20.467 --> 00:13:21.968
I don't know, mayor,

327
00:13:22.093 --> 00:13:23.470
I don't think it's
listed on the program.

328
00:13:23.595 --> 00:13:25.305
They're increasing
in number, mayor.

329
00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:27.265
These are the vicious
turkeys I warned you about.

330
00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:29.392
It's true mayor!

331
00:13:29.518 --> 00:13:32.103
Those turkeys just
ripped apart my cafeteria!

332
00:13:32.229 --> 00:13:33.814
Whoa!

333
00:13:33.939 --> 00:13:36.441
You won't get away with this,
you bastards!

334
00:13:36.566 --> 00:13:39.110
Wow! Those are
some pissed off turkeys!

335
00:13:39.236 --> 00:13:45.408
Okay, people, don't panic!
Bring out the defense squad!

336
00:13:50.038 --> 00:13:51.623
We need more than that!

337
00:13:51.748 --> 00:13:53.959
They'll only come
back in increased numbers!

338
00:13:55.585 --> 00:13:58.213
Hey, Phillip,
could you pass the beans?

339
00:13:58.338 --> 00:14:00.131
Beans? Uh oh,
looks like we'll be

340
00:14:00.257 --> 00:14:02.050
at war with these
Indians soon.

341
00:14:02.175 --> 00:14:04.594
Wait, wait, wait.

342
00:14:04.719 --> 00:14:07.055
Here it comes.

343
00:14:09.057 --> 00:14:10.267
Aaaaah,
I crapped in my pants!

344
00:14:10.392 --> 00:14:12.143
Aaaah!

345
00:14:12.269 --> 00:14:14.521
I think you got some
spatter on Chief Running Wolf.

346
00:14:14.646 --> 00:14:16.565
I spattered his face!

347
00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:19.442
Now he's a smelly Indian!

348
00:14:19.568 --> 00:14:22.070
We'll be back to part 14
of the "Terrance and Phillip"

349
00:14:22.195 --> 00:14:24.531
Thanksgiving Special,
right after this.

350
00:14:24.656 --> 00:14:27.534
Hunger is an enemy
that we all must fight.

351
00:14:27.659 --> 00:14:30.328
These children
desperately need your support.

352
00:14:30.453 --> 00:14:32.581
Hey,
somebody get me out of here!

353
00:14:32.706 --> 00:14:34.875
This sucks!
So please,

354
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.960
call and adopt a child today.

355
00:14:37.085 --> 00:14:39.462
I'm seriously
getting pissed off over here!!

356
00:14:39.588 --> 00:14:42.090
You want some
more Cheesy Poofs, hon?

357
00:14:42.215 --> 00:14:43.884
Ya, I won da Cheesy Poof.

358
00:14:44.009 --> 00:14:46.845
Okay.
- Sweet.

359
00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:49.264
This is serious
bull!

360
00:14:49.389 --> 00:14:52.559
There has to be a Happy
Burger around here somewhere.

361
00:14:52.684 --> 00:14:57.606
Excuse me, I am a lost
little boy--Could you help me?

362
00:14:59.524 --> 00:15:01.568
Well, screw you too!

363
00:15:01.693 --> 00:15:04.321
What the--Who the hell
let all these flies in here?

364
00:15:04.446 --> 00:15:08.033
Hasn't anybody ever
heard of insect repellent?

365
00:15:08.158 --> 00:15:11.286
All right, everyone,
it's time to give out

366
00:15:11.411 --> 00:15:13.622
canned food to the poor.

367
00:15:16.082 --> 00:15:17.667
Hey, where's Cartman?

368
00:15:17.792 --> 00:15:20.378
I don't know. Do you
know where he is, Marvin?

369
00:15:20.503 --> 00:15:24.132
Looks like we have the turkey
problem under control.

370
00:15:24.257 --> 00:15:26.009
It's time to embrace
the spirit of giving

371
00:15:26.134 --> 00:15:29.095
with the canned food grab.

372
00:15:31.556 --> 00:15:34.768
Come on, hurry up.

373
00:15:37.854 --> 00:15:39.814
Grab a lot son.

374
00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:43.234
Happy happy Thanksgiving!
Let 'er rip!

375
00:15:46.279 --> 00:15:49.908
Come on,
grab those cans, little boy!

376
00:15:52.953 --> 00:15:55.789
- Come on, Kenny!
- Come on, son!

377
00:15:58.416 --> 00:16:01.169
Now, let's see all
the goodies you're going

378
00:16:01.294 --> 00:16:03.880
to take home to your family.

379
00:16:04.005 --> 00:16:09.469
It looks like he got a--
a can of string beans!

380
00:16:13.932 --> 00:16:15.183
What the--

381
00:16:15.308 --> 00:16:16.977
Dude,
the mutant turkeys are back!

382
00:16:23.233 --> 00:16:25.193
Okay people, move along,

383
00:16:25.318 --> 00:16:27.612
nothing to see here,
you looky-loos.

384
00:16:27.737 --> 00:16:29.948
I tried to tell you,
but you didn't listen.

385
00:16:30.073 --> 00:16:32.617
Gather around everybody,
and listen good.

386
00:16:32.742 --> 00:16:35.704
Go to your
homes and arm your--

387
00:16:41.584 --> 00:16:45.088
What the hell are
you supposed to be anyway?

388
00:16:45.213 --> 00:16:47.048
That's not
important right now.

389
00:16:47.173 --> 00:16:49.551
No! What the hell is this
little thing supposed to be?

390
00:16:49.676 --> 00:16:51.094
It doesn't look like anything.

391
00:16:51.219 --> 00:16:53.638
Chef, the turkeys!
- Oh, All right.

392
00:16:53.763 --> 00:16:56.057
Listen up everybody,
and listen good.

393
00:16:56.182 --> 00:16:57.851
Go to your homes

394
00:16:57.976 --> 00:17:00.353
and arm yourselves
with whatever you can.

395
00:17:00.478 --> 00:17:05.525
We'll meet back here
in 15 minutes. Hurry!

396
00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:07.318
We are not going
to let our Thanksgiving

397
00:17:07.444 --> 00:17:09.988
be ruined
by a bunch of turkeys.

398
00:17:12.407 --> 00:17:16.828
You guys, seriously,
I'm hungry.

399
00:17:16.953 --> 00:17:19.164
I have to eat.

400
00:17:19.289 --> 00:17:21.249
Ah, sweet!
The Red Cross!

401
00:17:21.374 --> 00:17:24.669
I'll have fried chicken and a
side of mashed potatoes please.

402
00:17:24.794 --> 00:17:26.504
Sorry, kid,
but we're out of food.

403
00:17:26.629 --> 00:17:27.881
We ran out of funding.

404
00:17:28.006 --> 00:17:29.174
What?
- We just didn't get

405
00:17:29.299 --> 00:17:30.425
enough sponsors back home,

406
00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:32.385
so now we've got
to pack it up.

407
00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:33.636
But I'm not
a starving Ethiopian!

408
00:17:33.762 --> 00:17:35.346
I have to get back home too!

409
00:17:35.472 --> 00:17:37.557
Sorry dude,
we just don't have any funds.

410
00:17:37.682 --> 00:17:40.310
Here, have
a Teiko sports watch.

411
00:17:41.895 --> 00:17:44.272
Weak!

412
00:17:44.397 --> 00:17:50.361
People, we all have to do our
part against the evil turkeys.

413
00:17:50.487 --> 00:17:52.113
There's too many of them.

414
00:17:52.238 --> 00:17:55.658
Come on! Where is
that Thanksgiving spirit?

415
00:17:55.784 --> 00:17:59.245
We can't stop them.

416
00:18:01.039 --> 00:18:03.792
Today,
you fight for your city!

417
00:18:03.917 --> 00:18:06.252
You fight for your honor!

418
00:18:06.377 --> 00:18:09.297
These turkeys will
continue to push until they

419
00:18:09.422 --> 00:18:12.509
have taken everything from us!

420
00:18:12.634 --> 00:18:16.054
These fudged-up turkeys
from the the crustaceous era

421
00:18:16.179 --> 00:18:18.098
can take our lives,

422
00:18:18.223 --> 00:18:21.851
but they can never
take our freedom!

423
00:18:25.146 --> 00:18:27.524
Whoo! Yeah!
Whoo!

424
00:18:44.791 --> 00:18:46.167
Here you go, turkeys!

425
00:18:52.257 --> 00:18:53.967
Does my hair look okay?

426
00:18:57.595 --> 00:18:59.973
Can't go on...

427
00:19:00.098 --> 00:19:04.102
need...
appetizer...

428
00:19:04.227 --> 00:19:08.398
I'm sorry, God!
I'm sorry I mocked poor people.

429
00:19:08.523 --> 00:19:10.859
I'm sorry I
wasn't more sensitive.

430
00:19:10.984 --> 00:19:15.196
Please, please, God.

431
00:19:19.617 --> 00:19:22.162
My god has forsaken me.

432
00:19:35.049 --> 00:19:36.634
Huh, I wonder what's in here?

433
00:19:42.557 --> 00:19:46.561
Snacky Cakes!
Mmmm!

434
00:19:52.817 --> 00:19:55.904
Sally Struthers?
- Who the hell are you?

435
00:19:56.029 --> 00:19:59.532
Give me that cake!
- No, this is my cake!

436
00:19:59.657 --> 00:20:01.701
No, Sally Struthers,
you give me that cake!

437
00:20:01.826 --> 00:20:03.870
No! You can't have any!

438
00:20:03.995 --> 00:20:06.873
No, Sally Struthers,
that's my cake!

439
00:20:10.793 --> 00:20:15.548
You guys, Sally Struthers
is holding food from us!

440
00:20:15.673 --> 00:20:19.093
Uh-oh.

441
00:20:24.015 --> 00:20:25.808
Ahhh!

442
00:20:31.898 --> 00:20:34.317
Stay close, children.

443
00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:45.453
Oh, my God,
they've killed Kenny!

444
00:20:45.578 --> 00:20:47.288
You bastards!

445
00:20:47.413 --> 00:20:49.457
The last three are
getting away, shoot 'em, Ned!

446
00:20:51.417 --> 00:20:55.004
We did it!
- My God, what have we done?

447
00:20:55.129 --> 00:20:56.965
We've saved Thanksgiving.

448
00:20:57.090 --> 00:21:00.009
But all those poor turkeys,
they're--they're all dead.

449
00:21:00.134 --> 00:21:04.138
Every turkey dies,
not every turkey truly lives.

450
00:21:04.264 --> 00:21:05.932
As horrible as they were,

451
00:21:06.057 --> 00:21:07.767
they--they felt
like a part of me.

452
00:21:07.892 --> 00:21:10.311
Perhaps I shouldn't be
toying with God's creations,

453
00:21:10.436 --> 00:21:13.523
perhaps I should just--
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

454
00:21:13.648 --> 00:21:15.400
Excuse me sir,
we're looking for a little

455
00:21:15.525 --> 00:21:17.568
starving Ethiopian boy
who was accidentally delivered

456
00:21:17.694 --> 00:21:19.737
to South Park instead
of a Teiko sports watch.

457
00:21:19.862 --> 00:21:21.906
Have you seen anyone
fitting this description.

458
00:21:22.031 --> 00:21:25.159
Oh, that could be a hundred
kids in this town, mister.

459
00:21:27.161 --> 00:21:30.415
There you are.
Are you ready to go home now?

460
00:21:40.717 --> 00:21:42.593
Wow,
it sucks he has to leave.

461
00:21:42.719 --> 00:21:45.013
Yeah, I like him
a lot more than Cartman.

462
00:21:45.138 --> 00:21:47.140
You know, I think
I've learned something today.

463
00:21:47.265 --> 00:21:49.726
It's really easy not to think
of images on TV as real people.

464
00:21:49.851 --> 00:21:51.519
But they are.

465
00:21:51.644 --> 00:21:53.271
That's why it's easy
to ignore those commercials,

466
00:21:53.396 --> 00:21:55.481
but, people on TV are
just as real as you or I.

467
00:21:55.606 --> 00:21:57.358
Yeah.

468
00:21:57.483 --> 00:21:59.652
And that means that
MacGyver is a real person too.

469
00:21:59.777 --> 00:22:02.739
We're terribly sorry
about the mix-up, little boy.

470
00:22:02.864 --> 00:22:04.699
We'll get you
back home immediately.

471
00:22:04.824 --> 00:22:06.617
That's right you will,
God damn it.

472
00:22:06.743 --> 00:22:08.911
Move it povs,
I'm an American!

473
00:22:34.687 --> 00:22:36.522
Lord, on this day of thanks,

474
00:22:36.647 --> 00:22:39.192
we would like to extend
our deepest gratitude for this

475
00:22:39.317 --> 00:22:41.819
incredible bounty
of green beans

476
00:22:41.944 --> 00:22:44.072
you have
bestowed upon us.

477
00:22:44.197 --> 00:22:46.324
And though for some
reason you found it necessary

478
00:22:46.449 --> 00:22:49.452
to take our son from us,
and though you for some reason

479
00:22:49.577 --> 00:22:53.873
find pleasure in watching us
suffer, still, we give thanks.

480
00:22:53.998 --> 00:22:57.168
Amen.
- Amen.

481
00:22:57.293 --> 00:23:00.338
Does anybody
have a can opener?

482
00:23:00.463 --> 00:23:02.673
God Damn-it.

